    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite (a single `AcceptanceTest`) is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a derived, read-only `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 `telephone` for humans, while leaving `telephone` as raw E.164.\n\n**Three changes**, following the existing derived-field pattern in this codebase:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `telephoneDisplay` (read-only string) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\n2. **`Telephones.java`** \u2014 Made the class `public` and added a `public static String toDisplay(String e164)` that splits off the recognised country code (`+61`, `+1`) and groups the national digits in threes (`+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`). Null/non-E.164 values pass through unchanged.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression populating `telephoneDisplay` from `Telephones.toDisplay(owner.getTelephone())`, matching how `identityKey`, `locality`, etc. are already derived.\n\nThe `telephone` field itself is untouched, so it stays raw E.164. The new `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` test \u2014 which posts `0412 345 678`, then asserts `telephone == +61412345678` and `telephoneDisplay == +61 412 345 678` \u2014 passes, as does the rest of the suite (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
